# GraphQL fragments

Queries and mutations live under `app/graphql/`. Shared response fields live in `app/graphql/fragments.ts` as selection strings. Interpolate them inside `gql`. Do not paste the same field list again.

Check that file before writing a new operation. Use the closest selection, then add only fields that selection does not already include.

| Selection | Use when the payload is |
|---|---|
| `userSummaryFields` | A user from saas-api. Aliases `userType: role` and `revokeAccess: accessRevoked` keep the names components read |
| `userFields`, `userAuthFields`, `userInviteFields`, `userRecordFields` | Same as `userSummaryFields` today (the API has no clinic or medical fields); kept so importers don't change |
| `userSignInFields` | The user in `LoginUser` and `ValidateOtp`: what the redirect (including `onboarding`), role guards, and sidebar need before the reload. `FetchUser` supplies the rest |
| `projectFields` | A project, including `myRole` (gates the admin-only controls) |
| `scopeFeatureFields` | A scope feature row |
| `runListFields` | A run row in the queue: enough to poll its status |
| `runFields` | One run with its summary, network log and audit trail |
| `findingListFields` | An issue or finding row, with the issue stats; no evidence |
| `findingFields` | One finding with its evidence (`details`, steps, screenshot) |
| `emailLogFields` | An email log row (deferred) |
| `smsLogFields` | An SMS log row, including its user |
| `connectionFields` | `count`, `nextPage`, `prevPage`, `totalPages` |

Validate a new or changed operation against the API's committed `schema.graphql` (`qa-agent-backend/schema.graphql`) before shipping it.

```ts
import { userRecordFields } from '../fragments';

export const EXAMPLE = gql`
  mutation Example {
    example {
      user {
        ${userRecordFields}
      }
    }
  }
`;
```

If the same object shows up in a second operation and no selection fits, add one to `app/graphql/fragments.ts` and reuse it. Keep new selections composed from the smaller ones (`userFields` builds on `userSummaryFields`).

Do not add `fragment … on SomeType` until the schema type name is known.
